# Playnite themes (monorepo policy)

## Shape: every theme is standalone

- A theme is an add-on with **`"kind": "theme"`** in **`src/extensions.json`**, laid out like the plugins:
  - `src/<Theme>/AGENTS.md` — the theme's notes (sources, tokens, shell, components, deviations, what is unverified).
  - `src/<Theme>/info/` — `theme.yaml`, `InstallerManifest.yaml`, `danitesler_<key>.yaml`, `icon.png`, `LICENSE-*.txt` for everything bundled (Playnite's Default theme, icon sets).
  - `src/<Theme>/src/` — the XAML the theme ships, at Playnite's Default-theme paths, plus `tokens.css` and `Constants.template.xaml`.
- Profile fields: **`themeSource`** (`src/<Theme>/src`), **`resourcePrefix`** (the design system's name, PascalCase), `extensionManifest` (`info/theme.yaml`), `outputPath` (`artifacts/builds/<key>`), `requiredApiVersion` = the **theme API** version. Packages are **`.pthm`**; database `Type` is **`ThemeDesktop`** / **`ThemeFullscreen`**.
- **No shared kits, no inheritance between themes.** A theme never reads another theme's files; nothing is copied in at build time except its own `src/` and `info/LICENSE*.txt`. Other themes are only a reference for *Playnite mechanics* (which parts a view needs, how a trigger has to be wired), never a source of styles to copy.
- Build output is generated: `src/` copied, `Constants.xaml` rendered from `Constants.template.xaml` + `tokens.css`, licenses and `theme.yaml` added. Edit sources, never **`artifacts/builds/`**.

## Design-system fidelity

- **Name things the way the design system does.** Tokens keep their source names in `tokens.css` (verbatim CSS variables, or the package's token names); XAML keys are those names with the prefix: `bgColor-default` → `PrimerBgColorDefaultBrush`, `colorNeutralBackground1` → `FluentNeutralBackground1Brush`, `theme.palette.primary.main` → `MuiPrimaryMainBrush`. Component keys use the system's component names (`PrimerActionListItemPadding`, `FluentMenuPopoverPadding`, `ChakraBgPanel`). The build rejects any added key that does not start with `resourcePrefix`.
- **Map by role, not by color.** One source color can be several tokens (Fluent's compound brand is a fill, a stroke and a foreground); use the token the component spec names for that property.
- **Take specs from the source**: the design system's published tokens and component styles (npm packages, official docs), pinned to a version recorded in the theme's `AGENTS.md`. Write the spec in each file's header comment (component name, tokens, sizes).
- **A design system is more than colors**: its spacing (`Common.xaml`), its shell (how it lays out an app), its icon set (`Media.xaml`) and its component shapes. Where WPF or Playnite can't follow the spec, list it under "Deviations" in `AGENTS.md`.

## How Playnite loads a theme (drives the hard rules)

Source: `source/Playnite/Themes.cs` (`ThemeManager.ApplyTheme`).

1. Only XAML whose relative path matches a file in Playnite's **Default** theme is loaded (`scripts/data/playnite-theme-api.json`); anything else is ignored.
2. Each theme file is first parsed **on its own**, with only Default resources present.
3. Files then merge in pairs, `Default/A.xaml` then `Theme/A.xaml`, in API order: `Constants.xaml`, `Common.xaml`, `Media.xaml`, `DefaultControls/*`, `CustomControls/*`, `DerivedStyles/*`, `Views/*`. The later definition of a key wins.
4. `Toolbox pack` skips any `Fonts/` folder and any file identical to the Default copy.

## Hard rules (Playnite fails silently otherwise)

- Theme files are **overlays**: only restyled keys. Keep every `PART_*` and every part Playnite code dereferences (`SearchBox` needs all of `PART_SeachIcon`, `PART_TextInpuText`, `PART_ClearTextIcon`). Start from the Default file at the snapshot's Playnite tag; change visuals and layout, not behavior.
- Theme keys via **`DynamicResource`**. **`StaticResource`** only for Playnite keys or keys defined earlier in the same file.
- `StaticResource {x:Type ContextMenu}` in a later file resolves to the theme's own style (files merge one by one). Use `BasedOn` that way instead of copying templates (SliderEx, GameMenu, GameGroupMenu, TrayContextMenu, TopPanelMenu).
- When a Default style references a sibling in its own file with `StaticResource`, redefine both (`Separator` + `MenuItem.SeparatorStyleKey`).
- `BaseStyle` already sets Opacity 0.5 when disabled; styles based on it must not add their own `IsEnabled` opacity trigger (0.25).
- Focus: buttons, toggles, checkboxes, tabs use a keyed `FocusVisualStyle` (keyboard only). Text inputs draw focus on `IsKeyboardFocusWithin`. No `IsKeyboardFocused` border triggers on buttons (mouse clicks give keyboard focus too).
- No hard-coded colors in theme XAML: add a token and a template line.
- Icon resources Playnite copies (`Media.xaml` menu icons such as `AddGameIcon`, `PlayIcon`) are rebuilt from a `TextBlock`'s glyph and font, so a vector there is lost. To use the design system's icons, make each key a `sys:String` theme-relative PNG path (Playnite loads it through `ThemeFile`), rendered with `scripts/render-icons.ps1` from the theme's `icons.json`. Vector icons elsewhere go through `DataTemplate`s and the theme's templates.
- Slider: set `Track.Thumb` last (Track stacks parts in the order set). `ScrollContentPresenter` clips, so anything drawn outside an item needs the gutter as the panel's margin.
- No `DropShadowEffect` on popups or tiles; popups keep a 1px edge (WPF popups are layered windows). Wrap masked art (`OpacityMask`) in an element with `BitmapCache`.
- No `--` inside XML comments, no `{{` / `}}` in template comments, no **`Fonts/`** folder.
- Keep **`ThemeApiVersion`** as low as the theme allows (2.9.0 = Playnite 10.45+). Major must match Playnite's.

## Template placeholders (`Constants.template.xaml`)

| Placeholder | Result |
|-------------|--------|
| `{{name}}` | token color, alpha kept |
| `{{name@surface}}` / `{{name@surface@base}}` | flattened onto the surface (use for popup edges); a translucent last surface is an error |
| `{{name/NN}}` | token at NN% opacity |
| `{{a?b}}` | first token that exists |
| `{{name\|#hex}}` | fallback literal |
| `{{px:name[\|fallback]}}` | length in px (rem, px, var(), calc()) |
| `{{text:name\|fallback}}` | raw text (font names) |
| `{{TODO}}` | fails the build with "not mapped yet" |

Tokens are read from `:root` / `@theme`, and selectors containing `dark` override them. Errors report file, line and key.

## Commands

- New theme: **`.\scripts\new-theme.ps1 -Name "My Theme" -Key mytheme -Prefix MyDs [-TokensCss <file>]`**
- Build + checks: **`.\scripts\build-theme.ps1 -Extension <key> [-Deploy] [-DeployPath <Themes folder>]`** (also via `build-plugin.ps1`)
- Validate / package: `validate-extension.ps1`, `build-artifacts.ps1 -VerifyInstaller` (branch on `kind`).
- New Playnite release: **`.\scripts\update-playnite-theme-api.ps1 -PlayniteSource <checkout> -PlayniteVersion <tag>`**, then diff the Default theme for every file each theme ships.

## Versioning and releases

Same policy as plugins (**`playnite-extension-versioning.mdc`**, **`playnite-github-releases-per-extension.mdc`**): bump **`theme.yaml`** `Version` + **`InstallerManifest.yaml`** only when cutting a release; tag **`{key}-v{version}`**; one GitHub Release per theme with its **`.pthm`**.

